<title>DENMARK: Jyske Bank six-month 96 profit rises.</title>
<headline>Jyske Bank six-month 96 profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>					  (million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Group pre-tax &amp; extra items result  505 vs  397</p>
<p> Group net result			  371 vs  339</p>
<p> Net interest and fees income	1,127 vs  1,122</p>
<p> Securities and forex results	  159 vs  178</p>
<p> Losses and bad debt provisions	166 vs  158</p>
<p> Solvency ratio (percent)		 11 vs  11.1</p>
<p>Balance end-June 1996 54 bln crowns vs 47 bln end-June 1995.</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Denmark's fourth biggest bank is Jyske Bank A/S.  </p>
<p>It said in a statement that it maintained an earlier forecast for the full 1996 year of between 600-750 million crowns after adjustment for securities and currency fluctuations and extraordinary items. --Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom, 45-33-969650</p>
</text>
